    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1OROUTC4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 1, copy 4 of 7: same majority(A1, B1, C1) as T1OROUT, feeding T2H2N5.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_730eb5ef7a92444383217716aa9a0f64",
        "IdGuid": "a483e71a-7a43-4d2e-8cd8-b6850a91df96",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "79ddf4d4-4b2f-44b4-bbff-e1d05fa53b13",
          "05216c00-6f7f-45e2-9d30-4c8b7031d084",
          "b7d73e69-8ec8-40f4-b5fb-01226d1059a6",
          "a85dcac9-d87a-4d58-998d-7abfaf3abb19",
          "36a9bbd8-3061-4d3f-b158-97c396056dc1",
          "6d2d23d9-1739-4c04-9270-1664420a3c46"
